  "verbalization": "Hedaol B is shown to have a target relationship with Raji, which is then implicated in the target of multiple compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, Maplexin A, and terbutaline. All these compounds ultimately target DMS-273, suggesting a shared mechanism of action or a common pathway leading to the inhibition of DMS-273. The evidence indicates that Hedaol B may act through a pathway that involves Raji, which is a target of several compounds, and that these compounds may share a common target or mechanism of action in relation to DMS-273. The integration of these pathways suggests that Hedaol B could potentially exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the modulation of a target that is also targeted by other compounds, possibly through a shared biological process or a common cellular target.",
